# Tracer: release the full exact-domain Cartesian function-set definition.
# Before (rejected by the parser):
# release cart def cart(R,Z)
# Now: the complete checked equality is published and reusable.
# Boundary: cart(R,1/0), missing a coordinate, wrong order and wrong length reject.
# Gate: release litex -strict -f this file.

release cart def cart(R,Z)
cart(R,Z)={p finite_seq(union(R,Z),2):p(1) $in R,p(2) $in Z}
release cart def cart(R)
cart(R)={p finite_seq(R,1):p(1) $in R}
release cart def cart()
cart()=finite_seq({},0)

have A,B,T set
release cart def cart(A,B,T)
cart(A,B,T)={p finite_seq(union(union(A,B),T),3):p(1) $in A,p(2) $in B,p(3) $in T}

have D set={p finite_seq(union(R,Z),2):p(1) $in R,p(2) $in Z}
D=cart(R,Z)
have value D=(1,2)
value(2) $in Z
